    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Update a segment time range or duration.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id <SEG_ID[,SEG_ID...]> ... \r\n                              Target segment id; repeat --seg-id or pass a comma-separated list\r\n          --seg-type <TYPE[,TYPE...]> \r\n                              Target segment type(s): video, audio, text, sticker\r\n          --target-track <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Target track index(es)\r\n          --seg-index <INDEX[,INDEX...]> \r\n                              Comma-separated segment indexes within one target track, e.g.\r\n                              0,2,-1\r\n          --time-window <START,END> \r\n                              Select segments overlapping the half-open timeline window\r\n                              [start,end); start must be less than end\r\n          --in <duration>     Absolute timeline in point, e.g. 5s. Explicit unit required: us,\r\n                              ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --out <duration>    Absolute timeline out point, e.g. 10s. Explicit unit required:\r\n                              us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --in-offset <duration> \r\n                              Signed adjustment from the current timeline in point. Explicit\r\n                              unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --out-offset <duration> \r\n                              Signed adjustment from the current timeline out point. Explicit\r\n                              unit required: us, ms, s, or min; bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n          --duration <duration> \r\n                              New duration, e.g. 3s. Explicit unit required: us, ms, s, or min;\r\n                              bare numbers and m are invalid.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Set absolute timeline in/out points\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft segment time-range --seg-id <UUID> --in 5s --out 10s\r\n  # Change only the duration, keeping the in point\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft segment time-range --seg-id <UUID> --duration 3s\r\n  # Extend 500ms earlier and 1s later relative to the current endpoints\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft segment time-range --seg-id <UUID> --in-offset=-500ms --out-offset 1s\r\n",
